    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "I'm trying to define custom text objects for JSX attributes using mini.ai. The goal is to create text objects for the outer and inner parts of JSX attributes.\r\n\r\nI tried lazyvim [textobjects](https://www.lazyvim.org/plugins/coding#miniai) and they are working. In a similar way I tried to define JSX attributes treesitter object:\r\nlua\r\n```\r\n{\r\n  custom_textobjects = {\r\n    A = ai.gen_spec.treesitter({\r\n      a = '@jsx_attribute.outer',\r\n      i = '@jsx_attribute.inner',\r\n    }, {}),\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut I am receiving error message that textobject is not found nearby (even if I am). The specific error message I receive is:\r\n(mini.ai) No textobject \"aA\" found covering region within 50 lines and 'search_method = 'cover_or_next'.\r\n\r\nCould you please advise on correctly defining and using these capture groups for JSX attributes in mini.ai? The issue may be with the way I've defined the capture groups or if there's something I'm missing in the Treesitter setup for JSX.\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I'm trying to define custom text objects for JSX attributes using mini.ai. The goal is to create text objects for the outer and inner parts of JSX attributes.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I tried lazyvim <a href=\"https://www.lazyvim.org/plugins/coding#miniai\" rel=\"nofollow\">textobjects</a> and they are working. In a similar way I tried to define JSX attributes treesitter object:<br>\nlua</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"{\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    A = ai.gen_spec.treesitter({\n      a = '@jsx_attribute.outer',\n      i = '@jsx_attribute.inner',\n    }, {}),\n  },\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">{\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    A = ai.gen_spec.treesitter({\n      a = '@jsx_attribute.outer',\n      i = '@jsx_attribute.inner',\n    }, {}),\n  },\n}\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">But I am receiving error message that textobject is not found nearby (even if I am). The specific error message I receive is:<br>\n(mini.ai) No textobject \"aA\" found covering region within 50 lines and 'search_method = 'cover_or_next'.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Could you please advise on correctly defining and using these capture groups for JSX attributes in mini.ai? The issue may be with the way I've defined the capture groups or if there's something I'm missing in the Treesitter setup for JSX.</p>",
    "bodyText": "I'm trying to define custom text objects for JSX attributes using mini.ai. The goal is to create text objects for the outer and inner parts of JSX attributes.\nI tried lazyvim textobjects and they are working. In a similar way I tried to define JSX attributes treesitter object:\nlua\n{\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    A = ai.gen_spec.treesitter({\n      a = '@jsx_attribute.outer',\n      i = '@jsx_attribute.inner',\n    }, {}),\n  },\n}\n\nBut I am receiving error message that textobject is not found nearby (even if I am). The specific error message I receive is:\n(mini.ai) No textobject \"aA\" found covering region within 50 lines and 'search_method = 'cover_or_next'.\nCould you please advise on correctly defining and using these capture groups for JSX attributes in mini.ai? The issue may be with the way I've defined the capture groups or if there's something I'm missing in the Treesitter setup for JSX.",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": false,
    "closedAt": null,
    "comment_count": 4,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "LazyVim uses captures which come from 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects' queries. Basically, a curated collections of common filetype textobjects tailored to how certain tree-sitter parsers define their structure (node names, etc.).\r\n\r\nJudging by [this file](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects/blob/master/queries/jsx/textobjects.scm) for 'jsx' filetype, I'd try `@parameter.outer` and `@parameter.inner` instead of `@jsx_attribute.outer` and `@jsx_attribute.inner`.\r\n\r\nAlso make sure that the target textobject indeed can be seen within 50 lines of current line. If it is bigger than that, increase `config.n_lines`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">LazyVim uses captures which come from 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects' queries. Basically, a curated collections of common filetype textobjects tailored to how certain tree-sitter parsers define their structure (node names, etc.).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Judging by <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects/blob/master/queries/jsx/textobjects.scm\">this file</a> for 'jsx' filetype, I'd try <code class=\"notranslate\">@parameter.outer</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">@parameter.inner</code> instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">@jsx_attribute.outer</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">@jsx_attribute.inner</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also make sure that the target textobject indeed can be seen within 50 lines of current line. If it is bigger than that, increase <code class=\"notranslate\">config.n_lines</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "LazyVim uses captures which come from 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects' queries. Basically, a curated collections of common filetype textobjects tailored to how certain tree-sitter parsers define their structure (node names, etc.).\nJudging by this file for 'jsx' filetype, I'd try @parameter.outer and @parameter.inner instead of @jsx_attribute.outer and @jsx_attribute.inner.\nAlso make sure that the target textobject indeed can be seen within 50 lines of current line. If it is bigger than that, increase config.n_lines.",
