            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "I also wish to switch from `nvim-treesitter-textobjects` to `mini.ai`. I was also stuck here, right about to check `textobjects.scm`.  IMO, the error \"No textobject \"aA\" found...\" is misleading...\r\n\r\nQuestion: does _mini.ai_ also have jump action like in _nvim-treesitter-textobjects_ we can define keys to jump/move to the next matching capture? @echasnovski ",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I also wish to switch from <code class=\"notranslate\">nvim-treesitter-textobjects</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.ai</code>. I was also stuck here, right about to check <code class=\"notranslate\">textobjects.scm</code>.  IMO, the error \"No textobject \"aA\" found...\" is misleading...</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Question: does <em>mini.ai</em> also have jump action like in <em>nvim-treesitter-textobjects</em> we can define keys to jump/move to the next matching capture? <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/echasnovski/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski\">@echasnovski</a></p>",
            "bodyText": "I also wish to switch from nvim-treesitter-textobjects to mini.ai. I was also stuck here, right about to check textobjects.scm.  IMO, the error \"No textobject \"aA\" found...\" is misleading...\nQuestion: does mini.ai also have jump action like in nvim-treesitter-textobjects we can define keys to jump/move to the next matching capture? @echasnovski",
