                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> IMO, the error \"No textobject \"aA\" found...\" is misleading...\r\n\r\nMaybe slightly, but not completely. As there indeed no textobject can be found when supplied some not appropriate captures.\r\n\r\n> Question: does _mini.ai_ also have jump action like in _nvim-treesitter-textobjects_ we can define keys to jump/move to the next matching capture? @echasnovski\r\n\r\nNot as detailed, but [yes](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ea1af8c7d5e72148cae8a04e9887322a53fe66cf/doc/mini-ai.txt#L416-L418). Mostly designed for moving to left/right edge when inside the textobject.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">IMO, the error \"No textobject \"aA\" found...\" is misleading...</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Maybe slightly, but not completely. As there indeed no textobject can be found when supplied some not appropriate captures.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Question: does <em>mini.ai</em> also have jump action like in <em>nvim-treesitter-textobjects</em> we can define keys to jump/move to the next matching capture? <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/echasnovski/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski\">@echasnovski</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Not as detailed, but <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ea1af8c7d5e72148cae8a04e9887322a53fe66cf/doc/mini-ai.txt#L416-L418\">yes</a>. Mostly designed for moving to left/right edge when inside the textobject.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "IMO, the error \"No textobject \"aA\" found...\" is misleading...\n\nMaybe slightly, but not completely. As there indeed no textobject can be found when supplied some not appropriate captures.\n\nQuestion: does mini.ai also have jump action like in nvim-treesitter-textobjects we can define keys to jump/move to the next matching capture? @echasnovski\n\nNot as detailed, but yes. Mostly designed for moving to left/right edge when inside the textobject.",
