            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "> Not as detailed, but [yes](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ea1af8c7d5e72148cae8a04e9887322a53fe66cf/doc/mini-ai.txt#L416-L418). Mostly designed for moving to left/right edge when inside the textobject.\r\n\r\nahhhh... the `g[`/`g]` is similar to the \"move\" action.... Finally it ticks! Thank you!\r\n\r\n\r\n",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Not as detailed, but <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ea1af8c7d5e72148cae8a04e9887322a53fe66cf/doc/mini-ai.txt#L416-L418\">yes</a>. Mostly designed for moving to left/right edge when inside the textobject.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">ahhhh... the <code class=\"notranslate\">g[</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">g]</code> is similar to the \"move\" action.... Finally it ticks! Thank you!</p>",
            "bodyText": "Not as detailed, but yes. Mostly designed for moving to left/right edge when inside the textobject.\n\nahhhh... the g[/g] is similar to the \"move\" action.... Finally it ticks! Thank you!",
